  "description": "Follows the first three books of the Sanskrit Valmiki Ramayana and the beginning of the search for Sita, from Rama’s marriage and Kaikeyi’s two boons to Bharata’s regency, forest exile and the abduction. Examines competing meanings of dharma, Sita’s agency, royal promises, forest communities and the distinction between the selected Sanskrit narrative and later devotional retellings.",
